<main>
  <section id="hero">
    {% texy %}
      ### Services .[slogan]

      **What we do — and what it buys you.**

      We work in three modes: take a broken system over, make an expensive system cheap, or build a thin new one. Everything starts measurable and stays measurable.
    {% endtexy %}
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>The Hidden Cost</h2>
    {% texy %}
    **Where home-grown systems quietly leak money**

    01) **Systems rot in production.** Websites change, dependencies break, nobody notices until the data is empty — weeks later.
    02) **Platform teams burn hours on plumbing.** Your engineers maintain glue code and cron jobs instead of shipping product.
    03) **Cloud bills grow silently.** Unattended pipelines and over-provisioned services compound month over month.
    04) **Speed is an afterthought.** Slow sites lose conversions and rankings while the team tunes what it can measure.

    We've spent years being the team that fixes all four.
    {% endtexy %}
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Consulting &amp; optimization</h2>
      {% texy %}
        - **Legacy system takeover** — we step into systems nobody wants to touch. We respect the business value they've accumulated — no rewrites-for-rewrite's-sake, no big-bang migrations. First we pay down the technical debt: stabilize, document, version. Then the system starts earning interest on the value it already holds.
          <br>→ Debt paid down, value earning interest
        - **Distributed system optimization** — throughput, resiliency and architecture reviews for systems that hit a wall. We fix the cause, not the symptom.
          <br>→ Systems that scale without rewrites
        - **Cost &amp; lead-time optimization** — cloud bills, delivery pipelines and build times audited against real numbers. Every recommendation comes with a measured before/after.
          <br>→ Lower bills, faster shipping — proven, not promised
        - **Agentic AI optimization** — architecture and cost engineering for agentic AI: the right model at each step (small where it suffices), deterministic decision engines where a model is overkill, and self-hosted deployments for data that can't go to the cloud. We practice what we sell: our own in-house server cluster runs our AI experiments and client pilots. Effective in-house AI on commodity hardware — no million-dollar GPU cluster required.
          <br>→ AI that works on your sensitive data, inside your walls, at a sane price
        - **AI you can audit** — *a joint offer with our partner "Diversight.ai":[https://www.diversight.ai/]*. We design and run the agentic system: architecture, model selection, cost engineering. Diversight's human-in-the-loop specialists validate the data going in and the outputs coming out — edge-case review, annotation rules, an auditable trail. Human oversight is what the EU AI Act expects; this is that oversight, with evidence you can show an auditor.
          <br>→ AI with evidence, not vibes
        - **Web speed &amp; performance consulting** — audits and fixes for Core Web Vitals and real-user speed; accessibility as a requirement, not an afterthought.
          <br>→ Measurably faster, higher-ranking pages that work for everyone
        - **Long-term maintainability** — documentation, versioning, monitoring and handover built into everything we deliver.
          <br>→ Systems your team can own without us in the room
        - **DevOps &amp; FinOps** — CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, graceful migrations. We keep what we build running.
          <br>→ Fewer 3 a.m. incidents
      {% endtexy %}
